sudo /usr/local/sbin/radio_cli --help
Usage: radio_cli [OPTION...]
            Commands and options can be combined. The command: 'sudo
            ./radio_cli -b D -c 12 -e 17333 -f 33 -g -p -l 50' for example will
            boot up with DAB firmware, tune to the frequency with index 33 and
            the service with id 17333 and component id 12, start playing, print
            the service list and adjust the volume to a level of 50.
radio_cli - simple DAB radio interface to the Si468x for the terminal

  -b, --boot=FIRMWARE        Load the firmware and boot the Si468x. Use
                             argument 'D' to load the DAB firmware, 'F' to load
                             the FMHD firmware.
  -c, --component=SERVICE    Component id
  -d, --digrad_status        Prints the digital radio status. Prints the FMHD
                             status if in FMHD mode.
  -D, --station_text         Prints the station's text (e.g. songname) when in
                             DAB mode. Prints the radio text when in FM mode
                             (if available in RDS). Also prints further RDS
                             information when acquired and in FM mode. Use the
                             WAITTIME option to wait longer for a valid text.
  -e, --service=SERVICE      Service id
  -f, --frequency=FREQUENCY  Frequency index of the ensemble
  -F, --fm_frequency=FREQUENCY   Tune to a FM frequency in kHz
  -g, --digital_service_list Prints the digital service list of the ensemble,
                             including service data, only as json (combine with
                             -j). Prints the service list in iBiquity format
                             for FMHD.
  -G, --ensemble_info        Prints ensemble information (label)
  -i, --chip_info            Prints Si468x information
  -j, --format_json          Output info as json, if implemented. Use plain
                             output format for datastreams.
  -k, --shutdown             Shut down the Si468x
  -l, --level=LEVEL          Set the volume level of the radio to a value
                             between 0 (low) and 63 (high)
  -n, --event_status         Prints the digital radio event status. Prints the
                             FMHD event status if in FMHD mode.
  -o, --i2s_out=ENABLE       Enable (i2s_out=1) i2s as output - analog out will
                             be deactivated. To disable, use i2s_out=0. The
                             board must support his and custom kernel needed.
                             The Si468x must not be tuned to change this.
  -p, --play                 Play a station. Service and component have to be
                             given and the Si468x has to be tuned to the right
                             frequency already. Works also for FMHD (try
                             setting the service ID to 0 and component ID = 0
                             for MPS, 1 for SPS1, ...) if no other values are
                             known.
  -r, --rds_status           Print RDS status information
  -R, --rds=REGION           Enable RDS. Set the region -R U for US, -R E for
                             Europe. Use when powered up only.
  -t, --datetime             Prints ensemble date-time as ISO string
  -u, --full_scan            Scan all (European by default) DAB frequencies for
                             ensembles and save to the file "full_scan.json" in
                             json format. Command can be used with the json
                             output flag -j, but it will not print anything
                             until the scan is finished.
  -x, --next                 Tune to the next FMHD station
  -X, --previous             Tune to the previous FMHD station
  -y, --frequency_list=FILE  Get a frequency list from file. Give the file name
                             of the frequency list to use. The file must be an
                             ASCII encoded list of frequencies separated by
                             newlines. The list will be reset after a reboot of
                             the Si468x.
  -z, --waittime=WAITTIME    Certain commands (like RDS radio text) use a
                             timeout waiting for valid data. Wait for WAITTIME
                             seconds. Default is 1s.
  -?, --help                 Give this help list
      --usage                Give a short usage message
  -V, --version              Print program version

Mandatory or optional arguments to long options are also mandatory or optional
for any corresponding short options.

